      "Dribbling Rating": 5
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "2e41e0bb-8812-8161-94e2-c55edcfe817e",
     "fields": {
      "Display Name": "Theo Hedin",
      "Instagram Handle": null,
      "Images": [],
      "Overall Rating": 5,
      "Headline": "The absolute best blade you can get",
      "Review": "I’ve been switching around blades a bunch, and the Salming Trident in magenta has really grown on me — especially now that I’m trying to mix defense with stepping up and letting rip on goals.\n\nRight away you notice how light it feels. This thing is crazy easy to handle on the stick, almost like it disappears in your hand once you’ve got it going. Salming moved the balance point back in the blade so it feels lighter and more nimble when you’re dribbling or turning around defenders — which makes a huge difference when you’re back defending and suddenly have to sprint forward.  \n\nThe ball control is solid. The 8.5 mm concave and even curve make receiving passes and guiding the ball around players feel smooth. You can feel it right away when you do a first touch — it stays nice and predictable instead of jumping around.  \n\nWhen I pop a shot off, the blade releases the ball quick and clean. My hard shots don’t feel like they get lost in a mushy blade — you get that crisp snap you want when you’re ripping it from the point. It definitely feels like it helps give a bit more accuracy and speed compared to more control-focused blades I’ve tried.  \n\nThe downside is that, in super tight control situations, it’s just a tiny bit less forgiving than my old Q1 blade. Some passes don’t stick as long under the blade, so you really have to stay sharp on your technique. But honestly? That pushed my game a bit — you learn to be cleaner with the touches.  \n\nOverall, as a defender who likes to stay solid and then surprise the other team with a strong shot or carry forward, this blade feels balanced, aggressive, and just fun to play with. It doesn’t hold you back in defense and gives you that extra edge when you see a shooting lane. Perfect pick if you want a bit of everything without compromising on power and control.",
      "Anonymous": "with your name/ Instagram",
      "Passing Rating": 5,
      "Shooting Rating ": 5,
      "Dribbling Rating": 5
     }
    }
   ]
  },
